{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "label": "PersistentActor<Command, Event, State>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_initialstate", "label": "initialState()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "label": "onEvent(state, event) -> newState", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Bewusst synchron, waehrend onCommand async ist: ein Command entscheidet und Entscheiden macht I/O, ein Event ist bereits eine Tatsache und Falten ist Rechnen. Alles, was man hier awaiten wollte, ist genau das, was bei der Recovery nicht erneut laufen darf. state kommt aus dem Parameter, nie aus this.state - beim Replay laeuft onEvent losgeloest, bevor this.state zugewiesen ist, und das DevTools-Time-Travel-Panel leiht es sich genauso."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_oncommand", "label": "onCommand(state, command)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drei gueltige Ergebnisse: persistieren, ohne Persist antworten (read-only), oder ablehnen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persist_callback", "label": "persist(event, afterPersist)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Drei Garantien: das Event ist durable, der State spiegelt es wider, und eingehende Commands werden waehrend des Persist gestasht. Das macht persist sicher als Transaktionsgrenze - Seiteneffekte gehoeren in den Callback, der genau einmal pro Event laeuft."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery_flow", "label": "Recovery-Flow (Snapshot laden, Events ab seqNr+1 falten)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Waehrend die Recovery laeuft, werden keine Commands verarbeitet - die Mailbox fuellt sich und wird danach der Reihe nach abgearbeitet."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoverycomplete", "label": "onRecoveryComplete(state)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wirft dieser Hook, ist das ein gewoehnlicher Actor-Fehler und geht an die Supervision - kein Recovery-Fehler, denn der State wurde einwandfrei wiederhergestellt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "label": "onRecoveryFailure(reason)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine Benachrichtigung, keine Entscheidung: ein Recovery-Fehler ist so oder so endgueltig, der Hook waehlt nur, wer davon erfaehrt. Weitermachen kann der Actor nicht - state wurde nie zugewiesen und lastSequenceNr ist unbekannt. Das Stoppen haelt es sichtbar: wartende Commands werden zu Dead Letters statt im Stash zu verschwinden."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_journalintegrityerror", "label": "JournalIntegrityError", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Endgueltig statt Warnung, denn die Faltung IST die Recovery: ein durcheinandergeratener Stream spielt die Historie in einer Reihenfolge ab, in der sie nie stattfand, und laesst die Sequenz auf dem zuletzt gelieferten statt dem hoechsten Event stehen - danach scheitert jedes persist an einem JournalConcurrencyError, der auf ein kerngesundes Journal zeigt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotintegrityerror", "label": "SnapshotIntegrityError", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_journalconcurrencyerror", "label": "JournalConcurrencyError", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceid_validation", "label": "Was eine Persistenz-ID enthalten darf", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die ID benennt einen Stream und mehrere Backends bauen daraus einen strukturierten Storage-Key. Abgelehnt werden: leer (stiller geteilter Stream), > 255 Zeichen (Spaltenbreite und Primaerschluesselteil - Abschneiden liesse zwei IDs zusammenfallen), / oder \\ (Object-Storage legt IDs als Verzeichnis ab, a/b liegt in a), . und .. (Traversal), Control-Zeichen (IDs werden in Logzeilen interpoliert, ein Newline erlaubt geloggte Faelschungen). Komma und | sind bewusst erlaubt - der Offset-Store setzt Keys mit der ID am Ende zusammen, ein | kann also kein Feld abspalten. Lesen wird nie verweigert."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_assertvalidpersistenceid", "label": "assertValidPersistenceId", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_tagsfor", "label": "tagsFor(event)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wird einmal pro Event gefragt, auch innerhalb eines persistAll - ein gemischter Batch wird pro Art getaggt und bleibt trotzdem atomar geschrieben."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_eventadapter", "label": "EventAdapter (Schema-Evolution)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotpolicy", "label": "snapshotPolicy()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_payload_round_trip_rules", "label": "Was Events und State enthalten duerfen", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Getaggtes JSON-Tree-Format auf jedem Backend: Date/Map/Set/bigint/Uint8Array, BidirectionalMap (#1035), BidirectionalMultiMap (#1037), NaN/Infinity/-0 (#889), RegExp, URL, Error und Typed Arrays round-trippen als echte Instanzen. Error bewusst OHNE Stack - ein persistierter Stack wuerde Dateisystempfade in langlebige Rows leaken. Funktionen, Symbols, zirkulaere Referenzen und Promises werfen zur Persist-Zeit statt die Row zu korrumpieren."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_two_writers_for_one_entity", "label": "Zwei Writer fuer eine Entity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Sharding gibt genau eine Instanz pro pid - bis eine Netzwerkpartition plus Rebalance zwei erzeugt. Das Journal uebersteht das (Appends sind an die Sequenznummer gebunden), der Schaden liegt ausserhalb: der Verlierer hat onCommand bereits ausgefuehrt und beantwortet bis zu seinem naechsten persist Lesezugriffe aus veraltetem State."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_concurrency_loss_stops_the_actor", "label": "Ein verlorenes Rennen stoppt den Actor (kein Restart)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die Default-Antwort der Supervision auf einen Fehler ist ein Restart, und ein neu gestarteter Verlierer recovert den nun fremden Journal-Head und macht weiter, als gehoere ihm die Entity. Kostet nichts, kann aber den bereits gelaufenen Seiteneffekt nicht rueckgaengig machen."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_lease_fence", "label": "lease()-Zaun fuer Entities mit externen Effekten", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die Lease wird in preStart VOR der Recovery erworben - eine Instanz, der die Entity nicht gehoert, liest deren Historie gar nicht und kann keine veralteten Antworten geben. Der persist eines Nicht-Halters wirft sofort, statt den Konflikt erst am Journal zu entdecken."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_what_replay_rejects", "label": "Was der Replay ablehnt", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Prueft vor dem ersten onEvent, ob journal.read() dem Vertrag entspricht. Lehnt auch eine Historie ab, deren Anfang fehlt - wegkompaktierte Events, die kein Snapshot abdeckt: den ueberlebenden Rest auf initialState() zu falten wuerde einen Zustand erfinden. Nur ueber einen Snapshot hinaus kompaktieren."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_initialstate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_oncommand", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_oncommand", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persist_callback", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persist_callback", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery_flow", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery_flow", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoverycomplete", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery_flow", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_journalintegrityerror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotintegrityerror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_what_replay_rejects", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_journalintegrityerror", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_journalintegrityerror", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_journalconcurrencyerror", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceid_validation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_assertvalidpersistenceid", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceid_validation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_tagsfor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_eventadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotpolicy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_payload_round_trip_rules", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_persist_callback", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_persistence_persistent_actor_two_writers_for_one_entity", "target": "docs_src_content